msgid "STAGE_METTA_BHAVANA"
msgstr "Metta Bhavana"

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_1_GOAL"
msgstr "Observe your breathing."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_1_INSTRUCTIONS"
msgstr "You are sitting still and straight with your eyes closed, inhaling and exhaling as usual. Press and hold the matching button as the breath changes."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_1_BACKGROUND"
msgstr ""
"Welcome to Vipassana Simulator! "
"In Vipassana (insight) meditation, your goal is to experience "
"the ultimate truth through awareness and equanimity.\n\n"
"You have taken refuge in the Triple Gem, and you practice the Five Precepts. "
"Anapanasati (mindfulness of breathing) is a preparatory step "
"where you start by simply keeping your focus on your natural breath, "
"constantly observing whether you are breathing in or out."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_2_GOAL"
msgstr "Let go of all thoughts."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_2_INSTRUCTIONS"
msgstr "You continue to observe your breathing, but random thoughts hinder your focus. Release them by pressing and holding them."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_2_BACKGROUND"
msgstr ""
"Observing your breath seems simple enough, but in practice, "
"you will find that staying focused on it is surprisingly difficult "
"because your mind wanders all over the place. "
"You handle this by quickly noticing the distractions and returning to your breath.\n\n"
"Again, this is easier said than done at first, "
"but with practice random thoughts decrease in frequency."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_3_GOAL"
msgstr "Observe the sensations caused by your breath."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_3_INSTRUCTIONS"
msgstr "You now begin to focus on sensations. When a sensation appears, observe it by pressing the area before it fades away."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_3_BACKGROUND"
msgstr ""
"Now that you can keep your focus on your breathing, "
"you move your attention to the area around the nostrils and the upper lip. "
"There, observe the sensations caused by your natural breath. "
"Breathing in and breathing out is bound to leave impressions. "
"You may be surprised to feel sensations that you had forgotten were there or hadn't noticed before."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_4_GOAL"
msgstr "Observe the fainter sensations around the narrower area: the philtrum."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_4_INSTRUCTIONS"
msgstr "Keep on observing sensations by pressing the area where they appear, before they fade away."

msgid "STAGE_ANAPANA_4_BACKGROUND"
msgstr ""
"Your area of attention is now smaller in order to practice observing fainter sensations. "
"This is in preparation for Vipassana, where you will observe throughout the body. "
"By keeping the area small for now, you hone your focus towards faint sensations.\n\n"
"Also notice that sensations may be of any kind."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_1_GOAL"
msgstr "Observe the sensations of the entire body, part by part."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_1_INSTRUCTIONS"
msgstr "Observation itself is now done automatically. Drag the body to move the area of focus and observe every part of the body."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_1_BACKGROUND"
msgstr ""
"You now begin to practice Vipassana meditation and observe sensations throughout the body. "
"Starting from the top of the head as your area of focus, "
"you keep on observing sensations in the area and moving on to the next area until you reach the toes. "
"Then you repeat the entire process from head to toe.\n\n"
"It is advised that you always move the area of focus in the same order, "
"for instance, head, neck, chest, left arm, right arm, stomach, back, left leg, and right leg. "
"(But for this game, there is no need to worry about it.)"

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_2_GOAL"
msgstr "Avoid generating craving or aversion towards sensations."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_2_INSTRUCTIONS"
msgstr "Maintain equanimity by pressing sensations when they are neither green nor red."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_2_BACKGROUND"
msgstr ""
"It is crucial to remain equanimous when observing sensations. "
"Generating craving or aversion towards pleasant or unpleasant sensations creates clinging "
"and starts a process that ultimately causes a cycle of misery. "
"Every sensation that arises passes away eventually. "
"By realizing that they are impermanent and not reacting to them, you break the chain that leads to misery. "
"By practicing Vipassana, you practice being mindful of impermanence in your everyday life and finding peace."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_3_GOAL"
msgstr "Observe symmetrically."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_3_INSTRUCTIONS"
msgstr "Observe sensations in the same area on the left and right sides of the body simultaneously."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_3_BACKGROUND"
msgstr ""
"Now that you are fairly accustomed to Vipassana meditation, "
"you move on to observing both sides of the body simultaneously. "
"Instead of observing a part of the body on one side first, then on the other, "
"you observe the same part on both the left and right sides at the same time. "
"Not only does this make observation more efficient, "
"but it also serves as a step towards “free flow,” to be practiced next.\n\n"
"It is advised that you perform this only when both sides have similar subtle sensations. "
"Otherwise, and from time to time, fall back to part-by-part observation. "
"(But for this game, there is no need to worry about it.)"

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_4_GOAL"
msgstr "Observe as a free flow."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_4_INSTRUCTIONS"
msgstr "You are now proficient at remaining equanimous. Keep on observing sensations without interruption."

msgid "STAGE_VIPASSANA_4_BACKGROUND"
msgstr ""
"Acknowledging impermanence and maintaining equanimity, breaking the habit of reacting, "
"actually has the effect of dissolving gross, unpleasant sensations into subtle, pleasant ones. "
"In other words, your deep-rooted insecurities and complexes surface and fade away, albeit very slowly. "
"In this state full of subtle vibrations, you enter a “free flow,” "
"where you are able to observe continuously without blockage.\n\n"
"Keep in mind not to make this state your goal; "
"hoping for free flow directly goes against equanimity. "
"Gross sensations will keep on arising, which is more opportunity to eliminate your misery-bound reactions. "

msgid "STAGE_METTA_BHAVANA_GOAL"
msgstr "Share the goodwill with all beings."

